  ▌ sshpick inspect query ... [options]

  Show where a host resolves, as ssh sees it (ssh -G).

  Options:

       --json  Output as JSON


  Global Options:

  -h,  --help             Output usage information
       --no-color         No color mode (default off)
       --non-interactive  Never open the picker; connect only when exactly one
                          host matches
  -V,  --version          Output the version number


  Examples:

  - Show where a host resolves

    $ sshpick inspect stg-consul1

  - Inspect the one host that a query matches

    $ sshpick inspect new consul

  - Show the result as JSON

    $ sshpick inspect stg-consul1 --json

  - Read one field in a script

    $ sshpick inspect stg-consul1 --json | jq -r .resolved.hostname
